  "query_preview": "..\n(This evening through next Wednesday)\n\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW: An upper level high pressure system is \nshifting northwest, effectively cutting off monsoonal moisture. \nWhile afternoon storm chances persist through Saturday, storms are\nexpected to decrease in coverage and intensity each day. \nTemperatures will remain several degrees above normal, with highs \nin the upper 90s to potential triple digits while lows remain in \nthe upper 50s to low 60s. The hottest day is currently forecast \nfor tomorrow, with Heat Advisories in effect and a moderate risk \nof heat related illnesses in northern Nevada. Most models have \nthis pattern continuing through the end of the month, with the \nhigh remaining in place and suppressing moisture transport to \nNevada. The potential outlier solution, however, shows the high \nwobbling to the east as early as Tuesday, which would allow some \nmoisture and storm chances to return to the forecast area. This is\ncurrently a low confidence solution but would be an impactful \none.\n\n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS: High confidence in decreasing\nstorm chances through Saturday. High confidence in above average\ntemperatures and dry conditions Sunday and Monday. Very low\nconfidence in potential moisture return mid week. No changes made\nto base NBM output.",
